{"sections":[],"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"AppcuesKit"}],"role":"article","title":"Identifying and Managing Users","roleHeading":"Article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit"],["doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit","doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Identifying","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"In order to target content to the right users at the right time, you need to identify users and send Appcues data about them."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Identifying Known Users","level":2,"anchor":"Identifying-Known-Users"},{"name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Appcues recommends choosing opaque and hard to guess user IDs, such as a UUID. See the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.appcues.com\/article\/159-faq#choosing-a-user-id"},{"type":"text","text":" for more details about how to choose a User ID."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/identify(userID:properties:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It is recommended that the application identify a user at moments such as sign in, and also when the app starts up on a cold launch with existing log in credentials. This will ensure that any user properties tied to this user can be kept accurately up to date.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The inverse of identifying is resetting. For example, if a user logs out of your app. Calling ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/reset()"},{"text":" will disable tracking of screens and events until a user is identified again.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you have special security needs and your account has been configured to use the Appcues identity verification feature, follow the steps outlined in the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/docs.appcues.com\/dev-installing-appcues\/identity-verification"},{"text":", when calling ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/identify(userID:properties:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Identifying Anonymous Users","anchor":"Identifying-Anonymous-Users","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/anonymous()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The format of anonymous IDs can customized with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/Config\/anonymousIDFactory(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Anonymous IDs will always be prefixed with ","type":"text"},{"code":"anon:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by the SDK.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Grouping Users","anchor":"Grouping-Users","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Associating a user with a group allows you to additionally capture analytics at the group level, and target content to show based upon group membership and properties.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.appcues.sdk\/documentation\/AppcuesKit\/Appcues\/group(groupID:properties:)","type":"reference"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To ensure the most accurate content targeting based upon group information, it’s recommended to supply the group information immediately after a new user is identified.","type"